From: Jared <jared555@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 23:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix: watch only ask-password request files

The previous `DirectoryNotEmpty=` condition also matches residual `sck.*`
reply sockets. Those sockets can persist after `ask.*` request files
disappear (e.g. on timeouts or cancellations).

This causes repeated activation of the oneshot unl0kr-agent until
the systemd start-limit is hit, because the path unit immediately
triggers again on the remaining sockets.

Using `PathExistsGlob=/run/systemd/ask-password/ask.*` watches only
the actual password request files, preventing the retrigger loop
when only sockets remain.
---
 unl0kr/unl0kr-agent.path | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/unl0kr/unl0kr-agent.path b/unl0kr/unl0kr-agent.path
--- a/unl0kr/unl0kr-agent.path
+++ b/unl0kr/unl0kr-agent.path
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 Before=shutdown.target
 
 [Path]
-DirectoryNotEmpty=/run/systemd/ask-password
+PathExistsGlob=/run/systemd/ask-password/ask.*
 MakeDirectory=yes
 
 [Install]
